nt's check on the Turn after showing aggression on the Flop is a significant tell. They likely have a hand that's not strong enough to continue betting (maybe a missed draw, middle pair, or they're giving up on a bluff). With top pair and top kicker, I have a strong hand but not the nuts. Checking back here is the optimal play because: (1) it allows me to see the river cheaply, (2) it prevents me from building a huge pot when I might be behind to a set, (3) it keeps bluffs in their range on the river, and (4) I can reassess on the river based on the final card and their action.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
